[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own data says otherwise. The
reports were merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
"wrong date" is a symptom that three different bugs share.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: <code>parser</code> fixed ("fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
locales"), <code>hint</code> won't fix (booking-v3 form retired). Nobody has taken <code>one-day</code>,
and the parser fix does not reach it.
</Callout>

## The problems in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="zalun/mega-s01e03" tickets={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants whose locale writes the
  day first get day and month swapped (7 April becomes 4 July). This is the bug #4471 describes.
- **`hint`**: `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants type what
  the hint says, and the form reads it day first. Same symptom, different code: the form's hint,
  not the parser. Fixing the parser does not touch it.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day, not by a day/month swap. Tuesday becomes Monday, a
  client in Lisbon and one in Toronto get different days for the same meeting, an invite arrives
  before the booking. That points at time zones, not date order. The desk spotted these
  (`desk-notes.json`) but [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) still counts them under `parser`.

## What #4471 shows today

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table above already flags `hint` as "not this ticket", and its footnote counts the one-day
moves. The page around it still says one issue.

## How to tell them apart

- Read the tenant, not the intake tag. `meta.intakeTag` comes from the reporter's browser; the
  "tagged as" column above shows how often it disagrees with the tenant rule.
- Swap or shift: if the two dates in a report are each other with day and month swapped, it is
  `parser` or `hint`. If they are one day apart, it is `one-day`.
- `parser` or `hint`: a report through a `booking-v3` form is `hint`. Everything else from a
  day-first tenant is `parser`.

## Where each problem stands

- `parser`: fixed with #4471. [Ticket #1](https://github.com/zalun/mega-s01e03/issues/1) closed as completed.
- `hint`: won't fix, the `booking-v3` form is retired. [Ticket #2](https://github.com/zalun/mega-s01e03/issues/2) closed as not planned.
- `one-day`: not addressed by the update. [Ticket #3](https://github.com/zalun/mega-s01e03/issues/3) closed
  as not planned with #4471; if it comes back, reopen it rather than merging into a date ticket.

## Next

- New "wrong day" reports after 5 October: check swap or shift first (below the table above). A shift is `one-day`.
- Revisit decision 0001: matching on subject merged three bugs under one title. It has not been
  reviewed since June 2024.

